message: "If you use AmCraX in your work, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "AmCraX: Ammonia Cracking Simulation and Optimisation Platform"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Wee Zhern Ray"
repository-code: "https://github.com/weewzr/AmCraX"
url: "https://weewzr.github.io/AmCraX/"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-21"
keywords:
  - ammonia cracking
  - hydrogen carrier
  - Aspen Plus
  - process simulation
  - techno-economic analysis
  - heat integration
  - process optimisation
  - FastAPI
  - React
abstract: >-
  AmCraX simulates the decomposition of ammonia into hydrogen. It combines an Aspen Plus V15 flowsheet,
  driven through COM automation, with independent Python models for equilibrium, kinetics, heat integration,
  purification, techno-economics, carbon intensity and optimisation. A FastAPI service and a React dashboard
  show the results with a provenance label on every value, and a validation matrix records the checks against
  Aspen Plus and the literature.
